# Soroban Contracts

## Tooling & APIs

- Use current Soroban/Rust APIs and compile target `wasm32v1-none`
- Do not use outdated Soroban APIs or old WASM targets without verification
- Use `soroban_sdk::token::Client` for stablecoin transfers

## Approved State Machine

```
Created → Tokenized → Funded → Repaid → Closed
```

Cancellation allowed **only** from `Created` or `Tokenized` → `Cancelled`. No cancellation after funding.

| Function | Caller | From → To |
|---|---|---|
| `create_invoice()` | Freelancer | → Created |
| `tokenize_invoice()` | Freelancer | Created → Tokenized (SelfAttested) |
| `cancel_invoice()` | Freelancer | Created/Tokenized → Cancelled |
| `invest()` | Investor | Tokenized → Funded |
| `repay()` | Simulated Repayer | Funded → Repaid |
| `claim_returns()` | Recorded Investor | Repaid → Closed |
| `extend_invoice_ttl()` | Anyone | TTL bump only (no business state change) |

## Storage & TTL

- **Instance storage:** contract config and `InvoiceCounter`
- **Persistent storage:** per-invoice records via `DataKey::Invoice(u64)`
- Bump persistent TTL on every invoice read/write; bump instance TTL on create
- `extend_invoice_ttl` is maintenance-only — must not alter status, amounts, dates, or ownership
- Do not confuse business `due_date` with Soroban storage TTL

## Security & Invariants

- Preserve authorization boundaries (`Address::require_auth()`)
- Token transfers are security-sensitive; state changes and token ops must be atomic
- Enforce financial invariants: `face_value > 0`, `funding_amount > 0`, `funding_amount < face_value`, `repayment_amount == face_value`, future `due_date` capped at 1 year
- Every function touching `invoice_id` must validate existence or panic `"Invoice does not exist"`

## Events & Tests

- Emit `invoice_funded` events compatible with backend ingestion
- Every public state-changing function needs tests covering happy path, invalid transitions, and authorization failures
